From: disco-flying-wing-fpv
Subject: [PATCH] FirmwareManager: import a local firmware update file

Parrot no longer distributes the apps that updated the Disco, and its
update server may go. Let the application register an update file it
provides and has checked (FirmwareManager.importLocalFirmware): the store
gets a local entry for that model and version (MD5 computed from the
file), and the device updater offers it as if it had been downloaded.
---
diff --git a/groundsdk/src/main/java/com/parrot/drone/groundsdk/facility/FirmwareManager.java b/groundsdk/src/main/java/com/parrot/drone/groundsdk/facility/FirmwareManager.java
--- a/groundsdk/src/main/java/com/parrot/drone/groundsdk/facility/FirmwareManager.java
+++ b/groundsdk/src/main/java/com/parrot/drone/groundsdk/facility/FirmwareManager.java
@@ -68,6 +68,19 @@
      */
     boolean isQueryingRemoteFirmwares();
 
+    /**
+     * Disco FPV: makes a firmware update file the application provides
+     * (already checked by it, e.g. against known checksums) available
+     * locally, as if downloaded: the device's updater then offers it.
+     *
+     * @param firmware identifies the firmware (device model and version) the file contains
+     * @param file     the update file, kept where it is
+     *
+     * @return {@code true} if the file was registered
+     */
+    boolean importLocalFirmware(@NonNull com.parrot.drone.groundsdk.facility.firmware.FirmwareIdentifier firmware,
+                                @NonNull java.io.File file);
+
